### 2. A Better Approach: Database Normalization & Middleware

While the code above works, storing permissions as a comma-separated string in a `varchar` column is generally considered an anti-pattern in SQL. It makes querying difficult and is prone to errors. 

Instead, it is better to use a **Many-to-Many relationship** (a junction table) and move the permission checking into an **Express Middleware**. This keeps your routes clean and secure.

#### Improved Database Schema
